# Authentication & Sessions

- Choose auth by threat model: server session+cookie, OAuth2.1/OIDC, short-lived JWT+refresh, or mTLS/API keys for machines.
- Do not store access/refresh tokens in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`. Prefer HttpOnly + Secure + appropriate SameSite cookies.
- Short-lived access tokens; rotate refresh; revoke on logout/password/privilege change.
- New session id on login/re-auth (session fixation). TLS everywhere; consider HSTS.
- Authentication ≠ authorization. Passwords: KDF+salt (NIST SP 800-63B). CSRF for cookie sessions; tight CORS with credentials.

